subproblem.statement:
Assume (C1), the frozen statement of the sibling-of-parent node dor_imrep_massOn_eq_measure_and_support: for all P, n ∈ ℕ, open U ⊆ ℝ^P, T ∈ 𝒟_n(U) and every integer multiplicity triple R in U representing T, M_W(T) = μ_R(W) for every open W ⊆ ℝ^P, and spt T = U ∩ spt μ_R. Let P, n ∈ ℕ with n ≥ 1, and U ⊆ ℝ^P open. Let T, T', S ∈ 𝒟_n(U) and R ∈ 𝒟_{n+1}(U) be integer multiplicity with T − T' = ∂R + S in U. Let y ∈ ℝ^P and 0 < ρ < ρ' with B̄_{ρ'}(y) ⊆ U. Then there are t ∈ (ρ, ρ'), X, Y ∈ 𝒟_n(U) and an integer multiplicity triple RY in U such that:
- X is integer multiplicity and ∂X = 0;
- X(ω) = 0 for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U) whose support is disjoint from B̄_t(y);
- Y = T' + X, and RY represents Y;
- μ_{RY}(B̄_t(y)) ≤ M_{B_{ρ'}(y)}(T) + M_{B_{ρ'}(y)}(S) + (2/(ρ' − ρ))·M_{B_{ρ'}(y)}(R).
